cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "VIRAL: network topology, initial exposure and diffusion"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kefi
    given-names: Mohamed Bechir
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-24
abstract: "Independent simulation study of independent-cascade and fractional-threshold diffusion on Erdos-Renyi, Watts-Strogatz and Barabasi-Albert graphs of matched size and mean degree, with a second test on one anonymized real friendship network. Protocol v1.0 frozen 2026-11-24 with the owner's approval; all five registered experiments complete. Under independent cascade, Holm rejects 13 of 14 topology contrasts, 7 of 14 lie outside the smallest effect size of interest, and both contrasts change sign with the transmission probability. Manuscript version 0.2 is a preprint draft, not peer-reviewed. All results are simulations; no claim concerns real platforms or people. Developed with an AI research and development assistant (Claude, Anthropic), which is not an author. Repository URL: placeholder, not published."
keywords:
  - network diffusion
  - independent cascade
  - threshold model
  - small-world networks
  - scale-free networks
